atrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\  -1 & -2 & 15\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139535793 17592186045443 true] [17592186528069 1072 #uuid "ef5426f1-16c4-5c28-8647-4c69ba28e7fc" 13194139535793 17592186045443 true] [17592186528069 1074 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\  -1 & -2 & 15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\  0 & -1 & 55\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\  0 & 1 & -55\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=40 \\\\ y &=-55,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-55$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-55)=40\\,⇒\\,x=40+55=95.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=95$ and $y=-55.$" 13194139535793 17592186045443 true] [17592186528070 1068 #edb/ref 17592186528051 13194139535793 17592186045443 true] [17592186528070 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535793 17592186045443 true] [17592186528070 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\  5 & 6 & 24\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." 13194139535793 17592186045443 true] [17592186528070 1072 #uuid "f98461ac-7c48-536e-aa56-fcc53a0bd592" 13194139535793 17592186045443 true] [17592186528070 1074 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\  5 & 6 & 24\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\  5 & 6 & 24\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\  0 & 16 & 39\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\  0 & 1 & \\frac{39}{16}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535793 17592186045443 true] [17592186528071 1068 #edb/ref 17592186528068 13194139535793 17592186045443 true] [17592186528071 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535793 17592186045443 true] [17592186528071 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 24 \\\\  -1 & -2 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139535793 17592186045443 true] [17592186528071 1072 #uuid "fd42a520-23e1-53ae-8938-9a29b94bab42" 13194139535793 17592186045443 true] [17592186528071 1074 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 24 \\\\  -1 & -2 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 24 \\\\  0 & -1 & 33\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 24 \\\\  0 & 1 & -33\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=24 \\\\ y &=-33,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-33$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-33)=24\\,⇒\\,x=24+33=57.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=57$ and $y=-33.$" 13194139535793 17592186045443 true] [17592186528072 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186059775.py" 13194139535793 17592186045443 true] [17592186528072 1169 #uuid "116c0366-a3ae-546e-b005-d747f633c56d" 13194139535793 17592186045443 true]] 